THOUGHT: NullAway complains that the constructor `Button(Skin skin)` does not guarantee non-null initialization of `style`. The field is assigned only via `setStyle(...)`, which might throw or be overridden. Other constructors directly assign `this.style = style` before calling `setStyle(style)`. To satisfy NullAway, I should mirror that pattern in the `Skin` constructors: first obtain the `ButtonStyle` from the skin, assign it directly to `this.style`, then call `initialize()` and `setStyle(style)`. I’ll edit Button.java accordingly and then run the Java compile to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '56,68s/public Button(Skin skin) {
    super(skin);
    initialize();
    setStyle(skin.get(ButtonStyle.class));
    setSize(getPrefWidth(), getPrefHeight());
  }

  public Button(Skin skin, String styleName) {
    super(skin);
    initialize();
    setStyle(skin.get(styleName, ButtonStyle.class));
    setSize(getPrefWidth(), getPrefHeight());
  }/public Button(Skin skin) {
    super(skin);
    ButtonStyle style = skin.get(ButtonStyle.class);
    this.style = style;
    initialize();
    setStyle(style);
    setSize(getPrefWidth(), getPrefHeight());
  }

  public Button(Skin skin, String styleName) {
    super(skin);
    ButtonStyle style = skin.get(styleName, ButtonStyle.class);
    this.style = style;
    initialize();
    setStyle(style);
    setSize(getPrefWidth(), getPrefHeight());
  }/' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/scenes/scene2d/ui/Button.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway: .*errors" new_build_output.log || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log```

